  triage:title "Sprint doc D6a cites ATM-QA-AY-002, a triage record that does not exist, and conflates the roster-collision closure with the unrelated already-closed RBQA-AY1-F001" ;
  triage:description "quality-mgr qa-pr1310-r7 (PR #1310, AY.15 herdr-name-uniqueness, FINAL head 10bc123f8; report: PR #1310 issuecomment 5575994618). req-qa, arch-qa and quality-mgr (three independent passes) confirm no ATM-QA-AY-002.ttl exists anywhere in the worktree, yet docs/plans/phase-ay/sprint-AY.15-herdr-name-uniqueness.md line 183 (D6a) names it as a record this sprint closes. The same line names RBQA-AY-F001; the only matching-id record on disk is RBQA-AY1-F001, an unrelated, already-fixed docs finding about HerdrProcessAdapter::notify. The live defect the text was reaching for (collision-check algorithm duplicated between member_mutation.rs::preflight_roster_unique_names and roster_store.rs::enforce_roster_unique_names) is filed separately as RBQA-AY15-F001. Required correction: rewrite the D6a sentence to cite only records that exist under .triage/phase-ay/findings/ (AY-QA-001 for the HTTP_API_VERSION bump; drop ATM-QA-AY-002 and RBQA-AY-F001) and leave the duplication finding to RBQA-AY15-F001." ;
